{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed","id":398393,"title":"On Lunar Factions in 3rd ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-08T21:38:45-08:00","id":398393,"title":"On Lunar Factions in 3rd ed","content":"In 2nd ed, most splats had different factions. The Realm had their houses, their internicine intrigue and byzantine backstabbing. The Sidereals had their Gold and Bronze factions, and the independents. The Abyssals had the Deathlords, who might fight each other.<br /> This allowed you to do both your splat vs the outside, or your splat vs your splat, or your splat vs the world while infighting at the same time. It also gave you a bit of inspiration, especially the Dragonblooded Houses (in my experience, most dynast concepts can be 90% summed-up with &quot;I'm playing a House X, Y-aspected guy/girl who does job Z&quot; which makes it easy for people to think of characters).<br /> <br /> The Lunar factions did not do this. Frankly, I don't even know what the point of the Lunar factions. I suspect just because everyone else had them? They can't really come into conflict, because they just don't really have any significant differences.<br /> <br /> They had:<br /> The Wardens of Gaia: all Lunars want to safeguard Gaia, but we care about it slightly more than other Lunars!<br /> The Swords of Luna: all Lunars believe in defending Creation from the Wyld, but we care about it slightly more than other Lunars!<br /> The Winding Path: all Lunars, as per 2nd ed, are committed to the Thousand Streams River, but we care about it slightly more than other Lunars!<br /> The Crossroads Society: We are sorcerers. We do sorcery. What's our political goal? Uh, more sorcery for us?<br /> <br /> Then there's the Sun King Seneschals. Now, partly, they are the &quot;all Lunars want to defeat the Dragonblooded, but we care about it slightly more than other Lunars!&quot; faction. But they are also the &quot;we've spent a thousand years training all young Lunars to be perfect mates to people who are all dead and are never, ever coming back&quot;. It seemed a lot like the writers forgot that most Lunars had never seen a Solar or thought they ever would.<br /> Saying this, as badly written as they are, they're still the best faction because they might actually disagree with other factions, and there's a few different characters you can get out of them (guy who wants to put the Solars in charge, girl who wants to control the Solars gold-faction style, dude who found the Solars useful as a rallying cry and ideal but finds them really existing extremely annoying, girl who joined to enforce the Creation-Ruling Mandate and protect humanity from rogue Gods and gets really annoyed how suddenly the pro-Solar politics that was irrelevant before is a big thing, guy who joined to fight the Realm and thought Solars were awesome but finds them really disappointing in practice). Whereas being a Sword of Luna is no different to saying &quot;my guy doesn't like Raksha&quot; so it's not really a political faction at all, just a point of view.<br /> <br /> I don't know about other people, but I've never really seen any of the factions come up in games at all. The only time I've seen them ever come up was when I had the Sun King Seneschals offer to &quot;train&quot; (ie brainwash) the Solar PCs in my game (who turned them down).<br /> When I played a pure Lunar game, I don't remember any of the factions ever being mentioned at all.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think Lunar factions should be like in 3rd ed?<br /> Do you think I'm wrong and the factions are fine?<br /> Do you think the basic ideas are fine and they just need to be written better?<br /> Do you want to see new factions, and what ideas do you have for them?<br /> Do you think Lunars should just have regional power-blocs (ie factions like this pack of Lunars with this plan for the south-east and if you don't get on side they'll push you out of the region)?<br /> Do you think Lunars should have absolutely no politics whatsoever?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-09-2015, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T21:48:18-08:00","id":398425,"title":"","content":"I would have a hard time buying any Creation spanning 'society' of Lunars except one made up of sorcerers (magic makes talking with people on the other side of Creation doable). Other then that it should be regional power blocs and anyone with a reputation large enough to be heard of by a lunar in an entirely different direction is a big damned deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T21:57:33-08:00","id":398429,"title":"","content":"Ma-Ha-Suchi and his followers represent the political camp of &quot;destroy and conquer the Realm by whatever means necessary&quot;. They burn, pillage, rape, and send generations of &quot;barbarian&quot; cultures to die against the Realm's legions for the purpose of gradually wearing the Empire down in a few more centuries.<br /> <br /> There should be an elder with a camp of younger Lunars who believes in conquering the Scarlet Dynasty from the inside, with infiltration and assassinations and Dynasts turned against their own, to end the war with as little bloodshed and ruined infrastructure as possible.<br /> <br /> There should be an elder with a camp of younger Lunars (probably responsible for the Caul) who believe in building their own empire to rival the Realm for power and influence, forcing a stalemate that keeps both sides from ravaging each other any further, and hopefully conquering the Realm through trade, culture or symmetrical warfare over the course of a new era.<br /> <br /> There should be another camp who decided &quot;Fuck Creation, we're leaving.&quot; There shouldn't be much wordcount spent on these actors who have removed themselves from the stage, save for what your group might expect if you happen to run into them while searching the Wyld for something.<br /> <br /> There should be at least one Lunar who serve the Yozi, because Creation is such a hostile place for Lunars that turning it into a Hell Away From Hell seems like it can only improve the situation.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there should be at least one Lunar who serves a Deathlord (or the Neverborn directly)...or perhaps a Lunar so old that the Deathlord is an equal partner, perhaps even a spouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:07:42-08:00","id":398432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=398429#post398429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ma-Ha-Suchi and his followers represent the political camp of &quot;destroy and conquer the Realm by whatever means necessary&quot;. They burn, pillage, rape, and send generations of &quot;barbarian&quot; cultures to die against the Realm's legions for the purpose of gradually wearing the Empire down in a few more centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully with no Rutting Pens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There should be an elder with a camp of younger Lunars who believes in conquering the Scarlet Dynasty from the inside, with infiltration and assassinations and Dynasts turned against their own, to end the war with as little bloodshed and ruined infrastructure as possible. </div> </div> </div>Minimal bloodshed was Tamuz's thing back in 1e. He'd probably be a good choice for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There should be an elder with a camp of younger Lunars (probably responsible for the Caul) who believe in building their own empire to rival the Realm for power and influence, forcing a stalemate that keeps both sides from ravaging each other any further, and hopefully conquering the Realm through trade, culture or symmetrical warfare over the course of a new era. </div> </div> </div>Kind of goes in with what Ma-Ha-Suchi is doing, since he's trying to concentrate force to take down the Realm, and that's going to take a lot of force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There should be another camp who decided &quot;Fuck Creation, we're leaving.&quot; There shouldn't be much wordcount spent on these actors who have removed themselves from the stage, save for what your group might expect if you happen to run into them while searching the Wyld for something. </div> </div> </div>That was their thing for the past two editions. I can't imagine even minimal wordcount being devoted to this concept, since we're leaping away from it and leaping extra-hard. Like a 'Mech with 85% of tonnage devoted to mechanical jump boosters*, no room even for armor, final destination.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Total jump distance: 510 meters</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There should be at least one Lunar who serve the Yozi, because Creation is such a hostile place for Lunars that turning it into a Hell Away From Hell seems like it can only improve the situation.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there should be at least one Lunar who serves a Deathlord (or the Neverborn directly)...or perhaps a Lunar so old that the Deathlord is an equal partner, perhaps even a spouse. </div> </div> </div>Those wouldn't really be factions. The concepts seem a touch rarefied for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:14:06-08:00","id":398445,"title":"","content":"I have always thought it was strange that the Neverborn/Deathlords and Yozi only chose to go after the Solars and corrupt them to their side. Yes they did have that special opportunity to steal the Solar Exaltations form the Jade Prison, but what would happen if you stuck a Lunar in a Monstrance or somehow tied a Lunar exaltation to Lillun? I know this is getting away for the main premise of the thread, but I have always though it strange that only Solars have multiple flavours of themselves, while all the other splats are mainly unified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:17:39-08:00","id":398450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wardens of Gaia: all Lunars want to safeguard Gaia, but we care about it slightly more than other Lunars! </div> </div> </div>Meeh. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Swords of Luna: all Lunars believe in defending Creation from the Wyld, but we care about it slightly more than other Lunars! </div> </div> </div>A cohesive organization patrolling a border that encircles the entire world. Absolutely no way that could be a logistical nightmare. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Winding Path: all Lunars, as per 2nd ed, are committed to the Thousand Streams River, but we care about it slightly more than other Lunars! </div> </div> </div>What the fuck's a Thousand Streams River?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Crossroads Society: We are sorcerers. We do sorcery. What's our political goal? Uh, more sorcery for us? </div> </div> </div>Knowledge-sharing and favor-trading is something that helps sorcerers, which makes this the faction the most plausible of them. Not as a cohesive power bloc with an agenda, but just a sorcerous community within the Lunar Exalted (and possibly including some mortal sorcerers in apprentice or student-type roles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:19:12-08:00","id":398452,"title":"","content":"The Crossroads Society didn't really need a political goal. They were a sorcerous society. To the extent that they were political, it was along the lines of &quot;sorcery is an esoteric, specialized art that requires a lot more training and instruction than learning our native Charmset on your own does. As it is in the best interests of Lunar's everywhere to continue to have access to this powerful tool, we're going to club together and share knowledge, notes, and take responsibility for training up the next generation of Lunar sorcerers.&quot;<br /> <br /> And you know what, that makes sense as a faction. It works. It doesn't really have a grand goal, but not every faction needs that.<br /> <br /> The other 2e factions are definitely shit, though. I mean... I kind of, sort of see what they were going for with Swords of Luna and Sun-King Seneschals; the first was &quot;we want an organization for Lunars who are going to completely dedicate themselves to fighting the Wyld&quot; and the other was &quot;we want an organization that's going to be available for Solars to seek out or for Lunars who want to seek out Solars and work with them.&quot; Neither really... quite... worked. And the Wardens of Gaia and <i>especially</i> the Winding Path are just <i>dumb</i>.<br /> <br /> I do take issue with your characterization of the Sun-King Seneschals, tho. Their agenda wasn't &quot;training all young Lunars to be perfect mates to people who are all dead and are never, ever coming back.&quot; First of all, the Solars did come back. Second of all, hitching your wagon to the star of the Solars isn't exactly a dumb move. There was nothing subservient about it, tho. I mean, these are people who were looking to Lilith for leadership, and Lilith still hasn't made up her mind if she's going to slowly torture Swan to death or not.<br /> <br /> No, the dumb part of the Sun-King Seneschals was that it was a faction larger than a few Elder Lunars and some of the people they've personally trained. After a millennium, you kinda gotta accept that the Solars probably aren't returning.<br /> <br /> If I were going to re-do them, because &quot;faction of the Lunars that wants to ally with Solars&quot; makes sense, they would be a young, hungry faction that only just emerged; there should be very few SKS's who have been members of the faction for longer than three, four years, because it only became a politically viable stance once the Solars got back. This should be causing fault lines in Lunar Society, because some of the Elders who have managed to co-exist for years peacefully are suddenly now split between &quot;Yay, they're back! Time to team up and kick ass&quot; and &quot;Do you not remember the sickening monsters these people were?&quot; and points in-between, with the younger Lunar's not really getting the weird millennia-old grudges and damage at work.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more it seems to me this should definitely be a political faction of the Lunars with real numbers and clout. Just... done better the SKS's were. Because those guys were kinda lame, but the idea underlying them? Sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:33:47-08:00","id":398455,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget the Golden Widow Society.<br /> <br /> &quot;Find your soulmate, and EAT HIM.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:44:18-08:00","id":398460,"title":"","content":"Say, does anybody know whether the Silver Faction still exist in Third Edition ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:55:10-08:00","id":398464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=398460#post398460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, does anybody know whether the Silver Faction still exist in Third Edition ?</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>Q: To what extent are factional politics going to be emphasized in regards to Sidereals? While I'm sure the main focus will remain on the Prophesy Trio of Bronze/Gold/Can-We-Just-Do-Our-Fucking-Jobs-Please, will we see, for instance, interdepartmental rivalry as well? (It's friendly and constructive! Except when it isn't) <b>(Coikzer)</b></i><br /> A: They are still divided by Bronze and Gold Faction, which meant what it did in 1e. Other factions? We'll see. I have no interest in recreating the Silver Faction or some of the others posited in 2e. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T23:04:20-08:00","id":398466,"title":"","content":"I imagine in 3rd edition, Lunar Exalted will generally be divided into one of two groups - those who are actively engaged in war with the Realm and those who are not. You could probably consider the first to be the &quot;Anti-Realm&quot; faction, which would likely be the only thing you could consider a true &quot;Lunar faction.&quot; From there, you'll have smaller subgroups devoted to different things.<br /> <br /> These subgroups will probably revolve around a powerful/influential Lunar - Raksi may have a group of Lunars who help her out, or assist her, in exchange for magical training.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that Lunar society will revolve around ancient, First Age Lunars. Rather, any Lunar that gets famous or well respected could end up with a group of other Lunars tagging along and assisting or following him, and you could easily end up with a situation where a group of older Lunars end up following a young Lunar who just Exalted a few years ago, if that young Lunar has good plans, ideas, gets lucky, has useful contacts or whatever.<br /> <br /> I imagine that Lunar society would tend to praise success and action than simple age - so someone like Lilith or Leviathan may be given a modicum of respect for their ancient prowess, but realistically none of the Lunars are going to give a fuck about them because they're not out there doing anything. Meanwhile some young Lunar who Exalted 5 years ago and successfully drove the Realm out of a tributary would probably have a lot of respect and possibly other Lunars flocking to his banner.<br /> <br /> I would point towards something like Robin Hood as an example of how I imagine most Lunar &quot;societies&quot; might function - Robin Hood started acting as a bandit/fighting the king, for his own personal reasons, got pretty famous, and ended up attracting other people to his cause because they liked what he was doing. Ultimately, this is how I tend to imagine Lunar factions/society will be like - largely informal gatherings of people who follow a charismatic figure or ideal and work together, at least for a time.<br /> <br /> If one Lunar is successful at doing something, then other Lunars who share similar interests will probably take an interest in what he's doing.<br /> <br /> As for actual &quot;factions&quot; you probably won't see those, but there may be some things that resemble them...<br /> <br /> For example, you may have Lunars who spend their time traveling through the Wyld, the Underworld and Malfeas, exploring and understanding those realms. And other Lunars call these people, &quot;Nomads&quot; though these Lunars don't consider themselves any sort of united group (they're just individuals who like to travel to other worlds) and sometimes they get together and swap stories and tell each other what they've seen in their travels, and once in awhile some of them get together and travel around because they want company. But not really a &quot;faction,&quot; so much as a shorthand <i>label</i> for Lunars who heavily engage in one type of activity.<br /> <br /> Another one might be &quot;Infiltrators&quot; which would be a label for those crazy Lunars who sneak into Realm bastions, disguise themselves as Realm citizens and spend months or years &quot;behind enemy lines&quot; acquiring information or sabotage things. Sometimes they might work together, but most times they would just be individuals who happen to share a similar MO. It doesn't hurt for them to talk about things, but this group would be more of a fraternity than an actual organization or faction.<br /> <br /> And of course your &quot;Crossroads Society&quot; which is based around Lunars interested in magic, who sometimes swap information and facts.<br /> <br /> At the end the term &quot;faction&quot; implies a certain amount of organization, and more importantly, the idea of a shared, collective goal. I don't think any of these groups would have that sort of thing - it would just be a label for individuals who happen to share interests. When Lunars share a goal with another Lunar, they would probably end up choosing to follow or work with that particular Lunar (like the Robin Hood example). So again, the only real &quot;faction&quot; you would probably see is the one composed of the Lunars who are working towards the destruction of the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-09-2015, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:03:20-08:00","id":398512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed#post398393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think I'm wrong and the factions are fine?</div> </div> </div> </div>After Holden's swear-filled tirade, I don't think <i>anyone</i> here holds the position that &quot;the factions are fine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:14:12-08:00","id":398535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=398512#post398512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After Holden's swear-filled tirade, I don't think <i>anyone</i> here holds the position that &quot;the factions are fine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? I must have missed that, was it on RPG.net?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:19:58-08:00","id":398542,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to try to reorganize the Lunars into factions when we know their splat is going to be seriously reworked and reorganized and probably provided with 1-3 overarching goals in a way they didn't quite have before. Most likely 'fight the Realm!' and 'fight the Wyld!' are going to be among those goals, but it's not clear precisely why those will be the goals (other than pure vengeance of course).<br /> <br /> Factionalism will be,as others have noted, inherently limited by the high level of dispersion the Lunars seem to be stuck with. Sidereals are concentrated in Yu Shan and have always had superior travel tricks, something they will presumably retain, making it easier for them to function as a cohesive group. Dragon-blooded are concentrated in the Realm, Lookshy, and any place where they happen to be able to build up a lineage (something Lunars can't really do, beastmen are not in the same league as more exalts).<br /> <br /> Regionalized factions makes sense to me. The Abyssals and the Lunars share a common 'exalt suddenly, make crazy run to safe space' origin scenario, and the abyssal developed a regionalized structure based on the various deathlords (their safe space) they ended up working for. Lunars may end up in a similar clumped fashion, with every major Lunar clump having a 'support the mighty elder who keeps the Wyld Hunt at bay' and an opposing 'our mighty elder is bat****-crazy' faction, among others. it's just that Lunar factionalism may play out through regionalized subgroups of say, 20-30 Lunars loosely connected across a fairly broad geographical area, rather than across the whole of Creation and the entirety of the splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:30:52-08:00","id":398545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=398535#post398535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh? I must have missed that, was it on RPG.net?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the archives of Chancel Aleph, for your reading pleasure. (I suggest hitting up that site's writer quotes section, it's full of gems like this.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They don't make sense. Let's run them down, keeping in mind the whole time that Lunars are separated by vast distances and that the point of having a <i>faction</i> is to provide mutual aid, assistance, and protection to that faction's members.<br /> <br /> So we have the <b>Crossroads Society,</b> who are basically a bunch of silver Twilights. Okay, this is the one faction that gets a pass from me- they're basically a large, extended study circle, and they make sense in that context. They swap research and lore and sometimes get together to help educate freshly Exalted No Moons. They're like the sorcerers' clubs that have existed among all civilized Exalted factions through all of history.<br /> <br /> That's fine, and that makes sense. That's how sorcery and advanced mystical engineering work in Exalted.<br /> <br /> They don't really work in the sense of &quot;there are five big factions vying with one another&quot; or anything- but it makes sense that Lunars with that interest would talk to one another. So, okay.<br /> <br /> Then you have the <b>Swords of Luna,</b> who are uh, the guys what kill faeries. Okay, faeries are assholes, and they live in the same place the raksha do, so it makes sense that a lot of Lunars would spend a fair bit of time tussling with the raksha.<br /> <br /> But I mean, is that it? Do they get together to swap tips on killing raksha or\u2026? I mean, it's not really that their agenda doesn't make sense so much as that it's not enough to be a main agenda, certainly not set up against the other four. It just seems like a thing Lunars who live in the Wyld do, some of them more than others. This one isn't really nonsensical so much as unnecessary. It doesn't need to exist as a faction. They don't exactly have to roam far and wide and employ specialized methods to kill raksha, after all. They live right next door.<br /> <br /> Also, until very recently, you <i>couldn't run raksha as series antagonists</i> because they melted on contact with any kind of hostile Exalt. So you can't really build a game around the Swords of Luna- no recurring NPCs, just an endless mook-killing exercise. Hell with that.<br /> <br /> These days, the raksha milieu is complex enough to make the Swords of Luna seem dull and thuggish.<br /> <br /> Okay, moving on, the <b>Wardens of Gaia</b> make no fucking sense. Is this just a Werewolf throwback? Why do Lunars care about preserving the natural world? Luna loves Gaia, sure, but you can count on one hand the number of living Lunars that have ever met Gaia. So she's just a peripheral mythological figure for them- that's a hell of a lot to ask to form a faction around.<br /> <br /> In their modern incarnation they're a kind of senseless mishmash of ecoterrorism and Wyld-mutant-centric Thousand Streams River\u2026 eh? What? What are they even trying to do? Why do they associate?<br /> <br /> The <b>Sun King Seneschals</b> likewise have all kinds of problems. One of their biggest issues is that they're consistently written to be idiots\u2014 either they're naive morons, or they're schemers in the vein of the Gold Faction only vastly less sophisticated. This feels like a clumsy sop to &quot;some people want to tell Solar-Lunar stories.&quot;<br /> <br /> Granted, they're the only faction that really makes sense AS A FACTION, but that still feels wrong\u2014 the bond is a very intensely personal thing for every Lunar, and it's been out of commission for 1500 years. It should have a much larger place in Lunar history than just &quot;the stupid faction.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, the <b>Winding Path</b> makes no sense. I mean, it's very simple\u2014 this is the Thousand Streams River faction\u2014 but why the hell is that a faction? Nobody's agenda gets in the way of theirs except I guess the Seneschals. But most of all, <i>they don't need to work together</i>. The last thing you want is another Lunar coming in and messing with your project. In fact, you want them to stay the hell away. The most these guys would do with one another is engage in a little quid-pro-quo trading muscle or expertise. That's simple one-to-one dickering, that doesn't need to be a faction.<br /> <br /> Basically all of the factions are focused on things that are either irrelevant or too small to be defining to Lunars or they just don't make any sense.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Edit: Hm. We seem to be missing one quote from Holden when he reread the 2E Lunar hardback and started spitting fire. Anyone have that one handy? It's one of my personal favorites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 02-09-2015, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:33:51-08:00","id":398547,"title":"","content":"I tend to base Lunar &quot;factions&quot; around the elders and their extended Packs, mainly because The Thousand Fangs Army sounded liike too awesome a name to leave in 1st edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:57:00-08:00","id":398562,"title":"","content":"The Thousands Fangs Army (and their Thousand Fangs Total Control Zone) do sound awesome.<br /> <br /> I hadn't seen that quote from Holden. I think I agree with all the stuff he said.<br /> <br /> I have to say, I've been pleasently surprised by most of what the devs have said about Lunars. It probably helps that Holden, from what he said, has actually played Lunars a fair bit.<br /> <br /> On the factions-as-elders. This is a very sensible solution. However it doesn't inspire any characters like the Realm &quot;factions&quot; (ie houses) or Sidereal factions do though.<br /> That's why I wondered if people had ideas for real Lunar political factions or groups that aren't just an NPC and his goons.<br /> <br /> I liked the idea that was brought up about groups of Lunars interacting with different realms of existence.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it would be best if the Lunar book said &quot;here are some relatively large groups of Lunars who work together, as an example and to use as antagonists for non-Lunar games&quot; and didn't try to have any large factions at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T01:13:42-08:00","id":398568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=398562#post398562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the factions-as-elders. This is a very sensible solution. However it doesn't inspire any characters like the Realm &quot;factions&quot; (ie houses) or Sidereal factions do though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>can</i> but the problems with the elders as-written run deep.<br /> My Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi actually have ideologies that a Lunar might still maintain in some form even after concluding that the lunatics are running the asylum.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T01:21:07-08:00","id":398594,"title":"","content":"Wait, Raksi has an ideology beyond 'I want to learn Solar Circle Sorcery' and 'I eat babies or whatever else seems like it would amuse me at the time'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T01:41:30-08:00","id":398598,"title":"","content":"The problem with lunar factions is the same problem we've seen a bunch of times already: every group or splat's agenda is (a) destroy Creation, (b) save Creation, (c) be petty and shitty and fail to get the big picture, i.e. that there is a weekly war to see if Creation will be destroyed this week. Nuance and humanity thus exit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T02:02:55-08:00","id":398604,"title":"","content":"There should be a faction that wants to defeat the Dragonbloods. they think this is the number one priority and that all Lunars should be actively working toward this goal, mainly by conquering and raising armies, discovering caches of first age weaponry to add to the cause or by infiltrating terrestrial strongholds and acting as spies and sabeteurs.<br /> <br /> There should be a faction that believes the Lunars should stay out of worldly affairs and work on their own spiritual evolution. They emphasize this by bonding with nature and hugging trees.<br /> <br /> There should be a faction that is awaiting the return of the reborn Solars so that they may once again take their rightful place as the Stewards or Creation. The Sunkings fit this bill.<br /> <br /> There shoild be a faction that emphasizes protecting creation from outside enemies such as the yozi, the deathlords, raksha and alchemicals etc. They would prefer to do this under thencover of darkness in complete anonimity.<br /> <br /> There should be a group secretly dedicated to the yozi. Most of them would be akuma or well on their way to becoming such. They would network with other occultists throughout the threshold and do their work in secret.<br /> <br /> And there ahould be a faction that wishes to see the whole shibang fall to oblivion because the exalted screwed the pooch and rather than see the grand machine called creation slowly crumble, they would rather push the reset button and hopefully creation will get a do over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T02:14:51-08:00","id":398606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=398594#post398594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, Raksi has an ideology beyond 'I want to learn Solar Circle Sorcery' and 'I eat babies or whatever else seems like it would amuse me at the time'?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did specify my Raksi.<br /> But in short I portray the Thousand Fangs Army as the kind of Lunars who are equally interested in their personal evolution, often in a way that other Lunars might strongly discourage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T02:26:46-08:00","id":398607,"title":"","content":"Oh, so you did, this is twice I've misread posts recently. Maybe I need to stop posting when it is so late (or when it has arguably rolled over from late into early).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T03:13:41-08:00","id":398629,"title":"","content":"What I'm hoping for is that each Lunar is kind of a faction unto themselves. They pursue their goals, and may work with other Lunars--but when they do, it's one of two things. Either an informal arrangement based on &quot;We have a common goal and get on well together, let's hang out and pursue it.&quot;, or favour trading where, say, Raksi puts word out that she needs this book from the Heptgram vaults and anyone who gets it for her could ask, say, to learn some Celestial spells, or for the services of a second-circle demon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T03:30:39-08:00","id":398638,"title":"","content":"Yeah, none of these 2e factions make sense as groups with drastically different agendas who are in fundamental conflict with one another (a la the Sidereals, Dynastic Houses). They're more like different interest and focus groups who aren't in competition or conflict with one another expect where there's limited resources to pursue their agenda or where personal politics intervene.<br /> <br /> Re: &quot;Wardens of Gaia&quot; - Environmentalism doesn't make a great deal of sense vs humans - I'd imagine it has more currency as against conflicts between spirit courts and lax elementals (all that Spirited Away / Princess Mononoke style environmentalism themes), etc. that trash the natural environment, or against the environmentally transformative depredations of the Deathlords or Fair Folk, but that's still not enough for a large group to focus on (it's not like a major problem of their age that requires anyone to be Captain Planet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T04:21:42-08:00","id":398658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed#post398393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, what do you think Lunar factions should be like in 3rd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mixture of differences in opinion about how they should conduct their war, differences about what the world should look like when the Realm and Sidereals are subdued, and certain relatively straightforward selfish power and authority interests.<br /> <br /> Like, Tammuz wanting control of Chiaroscuro isn't exactly a faction, but if there's a faction saying that certain Lunars should obtain exclusive control of certain territories, then he subscribes to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T07:02:27-08:00","id":398745,"title":"","content":"I've always loved that rant of Holden's, but I do feel he's a bit off-base with the Sun-Kings.<br /> <br /> There really, really should be a Solar faction. It doesn't have to be all &quot;let's be their second fiddles again, yeah!&quot; or even all that friendly towards the Solars. But the Lunars and Solars are supposed to be complements to each other, and even with the Solars gone for 1500 years, there should still be that bond there. Moreover, the return of the Solars is going to be a really big deal to two groups of Lunars; those who actually remember the Solars, who are going to be the most powerful and ancient of their kind, and those who dedicate much of their lives to warring against the Realm and the Sidereals, who are going to see them as natural allies and resources.<br /> <br /> I do take Holden's point that this makes them kinda seem like a less sophisticated Gold Faction, but there really should be a not-inconsiderably-sized group of Lunars who are pushing hard to start aggressively recruiting, training, and allying with Solars. My take on this is that they should be young and hungry with a tiny handful of ancient Elders, with the larger mass of &quot;established&quot; Lunars somewhat leery about sharing power with these new guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T07:44:05-08:00","id":398756,"title":"","content":"With only around 300 or 400 Lunars, I have a hard time imagining factions at all. I mean, unlike the sidereals, they are not part of a centralizing organization with billions of gods filling the other positions. Is 50 people spread all over a world bigger than our own something that can be called a Faction? Unless most of them are sorcerers, how do they even keep in contact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T08:18:16-08:00","id":398777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Above all, I'd strongly fuss about the Elders. They should be as &quot;out of the picture&quot; as Sidereal Elders are</div> </div> </div> </div>... so, not out of the picture at all, then?<br /> <br /> I'm confused. If you're a Sidereal, you work alongside your Elders and have probably met them multiple times. If you work in Yu-Shan, you literally work in the same building as them. If you work in Creation in a non-north direction, your immediate boss is an Elder and has probably given you direct orders a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:00:20-08:00","id":399119,"title":"","content":"If I never communicated with any of you ever again, I would still be interested in Exalted. I don't need an authority to enforce that level of similarity with anybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:12:49-08:00","id":399313,"title":"","content":"Consider this, the Sidereal aside and perhaps the odd really powerful Exigent, the Lunars have been the <i>only</i> Celestial-class (Can I still say that without someone crying foul? I dunno.) Exalt. While the Sidereals make forays into Creation, most of their drama is in Yu-Shan, the odd Ronin excepted. You're damn skippy that if I'm a Lunar, one of the most powerful wolf fuckers I know within a couple hundred kilometers, I'm gonna wanna know what is up with the few other silver bastards within relative arms reach of me is.<br /> <br /> Here's a proposition, Terrestrial Circle Spell that can pinpoint any Exalt of your splat. Maybe Celestial? Seems a bit out of reach then.<br /> <br /> So, all spread thin as they are, I can imagine Lunars being a lot like cities are being made out to be. In each direction we'll get sample of a few, alone or in a group of like-minded individuals or some antagonistic towards each other. I mean, if a Lunar does a thing and someone else likes it or doesn't like it? That's a resource they can use or can be exploited then.<br /> <br /> Is that someone an Exalt? Well then that's a problem. A lone Lost Egg and maybe his mortal posse are an area shaping force. An Exigent empowered by the mountain god who's temple you tipped over is a bullet aimed at your head.<br /> <br /> Is that someone a Celestial Exalt? Well, fuck buddy, your party of PCs is now standing between two archrivals, equally matched in raw power. And what kinda Exalt is that Celestial most likely to be? Most Siddies don't have a reason to care about you, <i>mostly</i>. They take their marching orders from Heaven and the Maidens, and they may have their own agenda, their plans exists on a sideways level from yours. No, your biggest potential problem as a Lunar, before the Solaroids came a marchin' back, was another Lunar. Or your greatest potential ally.<br /> <br /> You are damn <i>skippy</i> that a Lunar cares about where he is in relation to his peers, but only the ones close enough to matter to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:30:00-08:00","id":399357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=399313#post399313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a proposition, Terrestrial Circle Spell that can pinpoint any Exalt of your splat. Maybe Celestial? Seems a bit out of reach then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ew, no. God no. Hell to the fuck no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:32:45-08:00","id":399361,"title":"","content":"Mmm, well, just a suggestion.<br /> <br /> I certainly hope that doesn't become the point of focus of my whole post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:45:19-08:00","id":399376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, all spread thin as they are, I can imagine Lunars being a lot like cities are being made out to be. In each direction we'll get sample of a few, alone or in a group of like-minded individuals or some antagonistic towards each other. I mean, if a Lunar does a thing and someone else likes it or doesn't like it? That's a resource they can use or can be exploited then. </div> </div> </div>IIRC, it has been mentioned that their are a few more places where Lunars have gathered together besides The Caul. But it is the biggest one and most dedicated to telling the Sidereal and their Dragon Blooded puppets to go **** themselves (they built a bootleg loom of fate and cut their nation off from the real loom out of spite).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:31:47-08:00","id":399415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=399376#post399376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, it has been mentioned that their are a few more places where Lunars have gathered together besides The Caul. But it is the biggest one and most dedicated to telling the Sidereal and their Dragon Blooded puppets to go **** themselves (they built a bootleg loom of fate and cut their nation off from the real loom out of spite).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not really spite, I don't think. Cutting yourself off from the tool the Sidereals have been using in the ongoing rolling attempted cultural genocide of your people and the successful cultural genocide of the Solars seems like it is just good sense.<br /> <br /> (I am super fucking excited about the Caul. More than just about anything else.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:48:10-08:00","id":399530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=399119#post399119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I never communicated with any of you ever again, I would still be interested in Exalted. I don't need an authority to enforce that level of similarity with anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that just makes you another Exalted fan, not a member of some &quot;Exalted Faction&quot;. Anything worth of being called a Faction should likely have members with an agenda in common, as well as at least as <i>a few</i> particulars and/or commonalities to their methods of achieving it, or some means of coordinating their various efforts at least minimally.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;Lunars fighting to bring down the Realm&quot; might be a Faction composed of several &quot;operational cells&quot; in different point in Creation, with some degree of coordination to their efforts or similarity or complementarity to their methods. A bunch of Lunars who are pro-Solars, or nature defenders, or whatever, each in their own way because they are spread all over Creation with no means of communication with others (and, barring great reputations, no means of even knowing about these others at all) are just a bunch of Lunars with an interest in common, not a Faction trying to further its agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:35:58-08:00","id":399616,"title":"","content":"So you might have a couple groups the coordinate for reasons.<br /> <br /> The Crossroads Society is a study club. For an age, Lunars have been just about the only practitioners of Celestial Circle Sorcery in Creation.<br /> <br /> Team Fuck The Realm, formerly Team Fuck The Shogunate, is a big movement for which some individual Lunars are a part of. Regionally, they would see each other as peers, would likely hear about each other or some third party also part of Team Fuck The Realm could bring them together. The third party doesn't even have to be a Lunar, elder or otherwise, could be a mortal, plenty of mortals hate the fucking Realm. I mean, fuck those guys.<br /> <br /> Lessee... what else? Can't really actively resist the Wyld, it's more of a local hazard.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T20:47:42-08:00","id":399911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=399119#post399119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I never communicated with any of you ever again, I would still be interested in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we'd miss you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T22:51:50-08:00","id":400016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=399119#post399119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I never communicated with any of you ever again, I would still be interested in Exalted. I don't need an authority to enforce that level of similarity with anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>No no no you're part of the Exalted faction. It sounds like you don't want to destroy the world tomorrow, so that's cool. The only question is whether your faction is fighting to save the world (in order to keep playing Exalted) or is too wrapped up in playing Exalted to notice that the world is about to end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:52:19-08:00","id":400090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=398432#post398432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of goes in with what Ma-Ha-Suchi is doing, since he's trying to concentrate force to take down the Realm, and that's going to take a lot of force.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see MHS's plan as more aggressive, and the Caul as more defensive.<br /> <br /> MHS isn't building anything lasting; indeed, he's tearing up lands and resources and peoples and throwing it all at the Realm to bleed it dry and then crush it underfoot. It's a very real concern whether his methods would leave anything left to rule.<br /> <br /> The Caul camp would be all about building up something lasting that can endure and serve as the basis for even further growth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T11:46:24-08:00","id":400592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=399313#post399313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a proposition, Terrestrial Circle Spell that can pinpoint any Exalt of your splat. Maybe Celestial? Seems a bit out of reach then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're going with this so have a counter proposition. Invert it from an Exalt finder into a homing beacon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:06:31-08:00","id":400635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=400090#post400090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MHS isn't building anything lasting; indeed, he's tearing up lands and resources and peoples and throwing it all at the Realm to bleed it dry and then crush it underfoot. It's a very real concern whether his methods would leave anything left to rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a concern to other Lunars. I don't think Ma-Ha would care. I seem to recall that his ideal endgame is a complete collapse of civilization with Lunar God-Kings ruling in the rubble. I'm not even sure if there's a nod to &quot;we should probably leave the Defense Grid intact and operational.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I am perfectly okay with this, by the by. There should probably be at least one Lunar Elder who is all about &quot;let it all burn, we tried civilization once and fuck that noise, never again&quot; and Ma-Ha kind of fills that role admirably.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:16:25-08:00","id":400655,"title":"","content":"On the subject of communication, I have used (or rather, had Lunar NPCs use) the following in my games. Sorcery, Artifacts, Familiars, messages given to migratory animals, messages given to allied elementals and gods, messages hidden in some mundane object or letter and then handed off to a mortal courier, messages left at dead-drops and checked at pre-arranged times, and in one case a Lunar would vision-quest to stay apprised of the next big gathering. I would imagine (and made it so, for my Creation) that the Silver Pact has members that derive their influence and importance from keeping track of their peers and facilitating lines of communication.<br /> <br /> &quot;I see you are researching <s>High Energy Chemistry</s> Essence-projection weaponry. Wipes-with-Pinecones was also looking into that. If you'd like, I could forward her comm frequency to you in exchange for <s>30 energy credits</s> a future favor...&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the factions themselves... yeah, what Holden said. I mean, their <i>concepts</i> are serviceable (except Wardens of Gaia, which completely suck), so long as you tweak them pretty heavily.<br /> <br /> For instance, my Creation has intrigues between the Winding Path, the Swords of Luna, and the Sun King Seneschals. The reason is that the most successful Winding Path adherents (Tammuz with the Delzahn, Rain/Python with Halta, Gerd Marrow-Eater with the Haslanti, etc.) are more concerned with building viable alternatives to the Realm than they are with destroying the Scarlet Empire. To the point where Tammuz is effectively an Imperial satrap, and others would like to avoid engaging the Realm at all. Many elders (who still seethe over the Usurpation), particularly among the Sun-King Seneschals, see this as tantamount to treason, and insist that the Thousand-Streams River should be a forward base for the eventual defeat of the usurpers / the restoration of the Old Realm. Both sides of the vengeance / coexistence divide actively court the Swords and the Crossroads Society, who take full advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:26:33-08:00","id":400682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=400592#post400592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where you're going with this so have a counter proposition. Invert it from an Exalt finder into a homing beacon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Near-entirely useless for the original idea of &quot;finding newly Exalted brothers and sisters&quot;, but definitely something with handy applications.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=400635#post400635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a concern to other Lunars. I don't think Ma-Ha would care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant as much, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I seem to recall that his ideal endgame is a complete collapse of civilization with Lunar God-Kings ruling in the rubble. I'm not even sure if there's a nod to &quot;we should probably leave the Defense Grid intact and operational.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I am perfectly okay with this, by the by. There should probably be at least one Lunar Elder who is all about &quot;let it all burn, we tried civilization once and fuck that noise, never again&quot; and Ma-Ha kind of fills that role admirably.) </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:37:33-08:00","id":400692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=400682#post400682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Near-entirely useless for the original idea of &quot;finding newly Exalted brothers and sisters&quot;, but definitely something with handy applications.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on the range doesn't it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:03:48-08:00","id":400740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love a good Lunar rant, so I feel I should add.....<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\">I'm perfectly cool with <b>all</b> the Lunar madmen. Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi can be pretty neat. Go barbarians.</span><br /> <br /> The <b>big</b> objection is the feeling &quot;these are the dominant people in the Faction&quot; and &quot;they are full Exalts, not ancient monsters (like Deathlords and Demons), with nothing but free time (unlike Sidereals)&quot; and &quot;anything I can do, they can do better - so resistance is futile&quot; and &quot;my character is a foot-soldier in <u><b>their</b></u> army&quot;. In the books, I get the impression that some of the weaker guys around them are young Lunars (not mere Beastmen) and I remember a few write-ups had characters sent on suicide missions by them (and it all snowballed into this feeling that Lunar stories must be Elder stories, about dealing with these old nutty people <i>regardless</i> of your concept).<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Infernals have Caerr - <i>a Barbarian</i>. But he's not defining the splat. Even if I'm not a Barbarian, he'd be a cool NPC to fight alongside, because he's not smothering other concepts out of existence (Gryfalcon seems to be just fine alongside him, taking on airboats in the North, raiding encampments and fortresses).<br /> <br /> Solars have the Bull of the North and a few other lesser known examples. But even with his age and power, we don't have 6-7 Yurgen's running around, giving us an ominous feeling that it's <i>their way or pick another splat</i>.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't care if Ma-Ha-Suchi wanted to destroy everything - hell, even help him - if it didn't feel he'd thereafter dictate what I do with whatever I try building for myself. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, I'm reasonably certain that Ma-Ha-Suchi doesn't even have a perfect defense going by scroll of exalts. I know that is probably an oversight instead of how it is supposed to be, but it really wouldn't be that hard for a combat focused non elder to gank him if he insisted on giving them ****.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:27:52-08:00","id":400792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/398393-on-lunar-factions-in-3rd-ed?p=400740#post400740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness, I'm reasonably certain that Ma-Ha-Suchi doesn't even have a perfect defense going by scroll of exalts. I know that is probably an oversight instead of how it is supposed to be, but it really wouldn't be that hard for a combat focused non elder to gank him if he insisted on giving them ****.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a canon character has ever had a write-up that actually explains how they are so successful, you know baring the ones that just have &quot;All (Splat) Charms&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}